cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "flybrain-reservoir: fruit fly connectomes as echo state networks, against random wiring"
abstract: >-
  Uses the wiring diagram of the adult male Drosophila central nervous system (166,700 neurons) as the
  recurrent network of an echo state network, drives it with market data, and compares it with control
  wirings that keep some of its statistics and scramble the rest. Replicated on the FlyWire female
  brain. Across the whole brain the fly's wiring remembers 8-11x less than random rewirings, and no
  wiring beats buy & hold.
authors:
  - given-names: Milan
    family-names: Kalajdzic
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MilanKalajdzic/flybrain-reservoir"
keywords:
  - connectome
  - drosophila
  - reservoir computing
  - echo state network
  - flywire
  - quantitative finance
  - time series forecasting
